          "require": "min(al*T - 0.04, 2.5 - al*T)",
          "prompt": "$x(t) = e^{-{{al}}t}$ (t in s) is sampled every $T$ = {{T|s}}. Where on the real axis is the pole of $X(z)$?",
          "answer": "exp(-al*T)",
          "unit": "",
          "explanation": "$x[n] = e^{-\\alpha nT} = (e^{-\\alpha T})^n$, so the pole is at $z = e^{-\\alpha T} = e^{-{{al}} \\times {{T}}}$ = $e^{-{{al*T}}}$ = {{exp(-al*T)}}. It lies inside the unit circle because the continuous signal decays."
        },
        {
          "id": "q6",
          "type": "matchPairs",
          "prompt": "Match each s-plane location to its image under $z = e^{sT}$.",
          "pairs": [
            [
