          "explanation": "$|z| = e^{\\sigma T}$ is below 1 exactly when $\\sigma < 0$ and equals 1 on the $j\\omega$ axis. $s = 0$ gives $e^0 = 1$, and $s = j\\pi/T$ gives $e^{j\\pi} = -1$: half the sampling frequency sits at $z = -1$."
        },
