          },
          "prompt": "The z-transform of $x[n] = ({{r}})^n\\cos(\\pi n/{{kk}})\\,u[n]$ has the form\n$$X(z) = \\frac{z(z - c)}{z^2 + d_1z + d_2}$$\nwith real constants $c$, $d_1$ and $d_2$.",
          "ask": [
            {
              "prompt": "Find $d_1$.",
              "answer": "-2*c",
              "absTolerance": 0.005,
              "explanation": "The table gives the denominator $z^2 - 2az\\cos\\Omega + a^2$, so $d_1 = -2a\\cos\\Omega$ = −2 × {{r}} × cos(π/{{kk}}) = {{-2*c}}. (The poles are at $ae^{\\pm j\\Omega}$ = {{r}}$e^{\\pm j\\pi/{{kk}}}$.)"
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Find $c$ in the numerator.",
              "answer": "c",
              "absTolerance": 0.005,
              "explanation": "The numerator is $z(z - a\\cos\\Omega)$, so $c = a\\cos\\Omega$ = {{r}} × cos(π/{{kk}}) = {{c}}."
            }
          ],
          "unit": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "q2",
          "type": "numeric",
          "params": {
            "a": [
              0.6,
              0.7,
              0.8,
              0.9
            ],
            "kk": [
              3,
              4,
              6
            ]
          },
          "derived": {
